60,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option C is the only logical choice. It solves the noise issue and the mess of eating in the office.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Option B... it would stop the outside hire costs. But the quote for the screen is quite expensive.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option A! Then we can have snacks and parties and everyone can help clean the crumbs!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option B offers a place for the difficult words to be spoken in peace, away from the prying eyes of the desk.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option B is the most efficient. It eliminates the outside hire costs and centralizes the utility of the room.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Rin, Option A would only increase the mess and the noise. It's a recipe for disaster.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Option B makes the most sense for the budget in the long run, even if the initial cost is high.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,But Option C is boring! Who wants to sit alone in a room? That's not an adventure!,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Servas,,"Solitude has its place, but we are currently too solitary. We need a bridge, not a wall.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,Option B removes the logistical burden of traveling to outside venues. It saves time and money.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, if you want efficiency, you'll agree that a ""meeting space"" with a thin wall is just a place to be overheard.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'm... I'm leaning towards Option B. It seems like the most practical way to stop the monthly payments.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'll vote for the kitchen! It's the most fun! And we can make a cleaning chart!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Servas,,Let us build a space where we can look each other in the eye and speak with honesty.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,The cost of the fit-out is a one-time expense. The cost of outside hire is a permanent leak of resources.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shion,,I will stick with Option C. It is the only way to ensure the office remains a place of work.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll go with Option B. It feels like the safest bet for the company's finances.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,Kitchen! Kitchen! Kitchen!,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Servas,,I cast my lot with the space that allows us to reconnect. Option B it is.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,Option B is the only choice that addresses the waste of hours and funds.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
